       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, which is 850 mg three times daily. This order is five times that limit, and a single 4250 mg dose is also far above any standard dose. At that level the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is the max standard dose of 2,550 mg/day.\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, if you intended a lower dose.\n- Another dose or frequency.\n\nIf 4250 mg is what you want, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it as written."
